# npm install output. Never committed; `npm ci` reproduces it exactly from
# the committed package-lock.json.
node_modules/

# npm/vite scratch output.
npm-debug.log*
.vite/
*.local

# NOT ignored, deliberately, and both are easy to get wrong:
#
#   dist/     web/embed.go embeds it with `//go:embed all:dist`, and a
#             missing embed target is a hard *compile* error, so an ignored
#             (and therefore absent) dist/ breaks `go build ./...` on any
#             clean checkout without Node. dist/ instead ships committed
#             placeholders, per the rationale in web/embed.go. `npm run
#             build` (i.e. `task web:build`) overwrites those placeholders
#             with real Vite output -- that shows up as a dirty tree, and
#             the build artefacts (unstably hash-named on every rebuild)
#             are not meant to be committed. Restore by hand with
#             `git checkout -- dist && git clean -fd dist`. loam-nvb.15
#             settled this: the top-level `task build` (Taskfile.yml) runs
#             `web:build` (real output, for the Go embed step to pick up),
#             then `go build ./...`, then restores the placeholders on an
#             EXIT trap -- so routine builds leave a clean tree, while
#             `task web:build` run on its own (e.g. loam-nvb.16, or to
#             inspect the real output) leaves it in place. See
#             docs/web-frontend-spec.md -> Build & Embed.
#
#   src/gen/  Generated TypeScript (protoc-gen-es + protoc-gen-connect-query,
#             landing in loam-nvb.2) is committed, mirroring the Go side:
#             internal/gen is committed and CI enforces zero drift by
#             re-running codegen and failing on a diff. Committing the TS
#             keeps `npm run build` and `npm test` working without a
#             codegen step, exactly as docs/web-frontend-spec.md -> Codegen
#             specifies, and lets the same drift check cover the web side
#             now that `task web:generate` exists (loam-nvb.15) -- CI's
#             generated-code drift check regenerates this too and fails on
#             a diff, the same as internal/gen.

# Playwright output (loam-li0.11.1). Both are runtime artefacts of `task
# test:e2e`, never committed:
#
#   test-results/      per-test traces, screenshots and videos on failure
#   playwright-report/ the HTML reporter's output, produced when CI is set
#
# These must be ignored, not merely uncommitted: CI's generated-code drift
# check fails on ANY `git status --porcelain` output, and porcelain lists
# untracked files too -- so an unignored artefact directory turns a passing
# e2e run into a spurious "generated code drifted" failure the moment the
# two ever run in the same job. Locally it just leaves a dirty tree.
test-results/
playwright-report/
